        "text": "**Illustrative ten-year value: $21,900, $444,100, depending on the scenario.** This is a very wide range, not a prediction.\n\n| Scenario | Published 2030 price range used | Illustrative value in 2036 |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Conservative | $300, $400 | **$21,900, $44,900** |\n| Middle | $400, $800 | **$44,900, $254,200** |\n| Optimistic | $800, $1,000 | **$254,200, $444,100** |\n\nThe calculation starts with NVDA at **$219.28 as of September 11, 2026**. Because the available published targets extend only to 2030, I assumed each target is reached over the next four years and that the resulting annualized return then continues unchanged for another six years:\n\n**Future value = $10,000 \u00d7 (2030 target \u00f7 $219.28)^(10 \u00f7 4).**\n\nFor example, the low end is **$10,000 \u00d7 ($300 \u00f7 $219.28)^2.5 = $21,900**, while the high end is **$10,000 \u00d7 ($1,000 \u00f7 $219.28)^2.5 = $444,100**.\n\nThese figures do not quantify an additional \u201cgolden-cross premium.\u201d A golden cross is a lagging trend-confirmation signal and can produce false signals; no published NVDA-specific ten-year golden-cross forecast was available. The estimates therefore assume you enter at the stated current price and remain invested. A strategy that sells after an opposite crossover could produce materially different results because it may spend time in cash and incur trading costs or taxes.\n\nThis is scenario analysis, not investment advice.",
